  "slides": [
    {
      "kind": "cover",
      "quote": {
        "text": "How do I know if my child actually learned something",
        "source": "searchedProblems[2].phrase"
      },
      "emphasis": [
        "learned"
      ],
      "promise": {
        "text": "How to tell if your homeschooler actually learned it",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/title"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "answer",
      "eyebrow": {
        "text": "In short",
        "source": "micro"
      },
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Covered is not learned.",
          "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/dek#0"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ask four questions a week or more later, write the answers down, and know when a result is not enough to say.",
          "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/dek#1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "step",
      "eyebrow": {
        "text": "Five ways to check it landed",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].heading"
      },
      "number": {
        "text": "1",
        "source": "micro"
      },
      "head": {
        "text": "Ask them to teach it back to you.",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[0]#0"
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "text": "If they can explain a step to a stuffed animal or a younger sibling, they understand it.",
          "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[0]#1"
        },
        {
          "text": "If they can only repeat a memorized line, they don't yet.",
          "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[0]#2"
        }
      ],
      "emphasis": [
        "teach"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "step",
      "eyebrow": {
        "text": "Five ways to check it landed",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].heading"
      },
      "number": {
        "text": "2",
        "source": "micro"
      },
      "head": {
        "text": "Have them narrate what they just read or did, in their own words, without looking.",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[1]#0"
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "text": "A summary that includes why something happened, not just what happened, is the stronger sign.",
          "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[1]#1"
        }
      ],
      "emphasis": [
        "narrate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "step",
      "eyebrow": {
        "text": "Five ways to check it landed",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].heading"
      },
      "number": {
        "text": "3",
        "source": "micro"
      },
      "head": {
        "text": "Ask a few oral questions that mix recall and reasoning.",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[2]#0"
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "text": "\"What's 6 times 7\" checks recall.",
          "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[2]#1"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Why does that work\" checks understanding.",
          "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[2]#2"
        }
      ],
      "emphasis": [
        "reasoning"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "step",
      "eyebrow": {
        "text": "Five ways to check it landed",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].heading"
      },
      "number": {
        "text": "4",
        "source": "micro"
      },
      "head": {
        "text": "Do a short spot check from the workbook itself: cover the answer, have them solve it again a different way than the book showed.",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[3]#0"
      },
      "body": [],
      "emphasis": [
        "different"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "step",
      "eyebrow": {
        "text": "Five ways to check it landed",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].heading"
      },
      "number": {
        "text": "5",
        "source": "micro"
      },
      "head": {
        "text": "Ask for a two-minute demonstration: build it, draw it, or show the step on paper.",
        "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[4]#0"
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "text": "Watching them do it catches things a spoken answer hides.",
          "source": "guide:how-to-check-if-your-child-learned-something/body[2].items[4]#1"
        }
      ],
      "emphasis": [
        "demonstration"
      ]
    },
    {
